      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's walk through Andréa's frustration and Colette's icy return step by step.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Tu Coucheras avec Moi Ce Soir?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Will You Sleep with Me Tonight?' Andréa reads the suggestive title of the first script on her desk.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Mince!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Darn!' The second script on her pile is yet another romantic comedy.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Amour et Muffins.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Love and Muffins.' Even the third script title sounds like a syrupy love story.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "C'est un complot ou quoi?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Is it a conspiracy or what?' Heartbroken after losing Colette, Andréa feels mocked by all these romance scripts.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Ça va?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Are you okay?' Camille asks if Andréa wants her to throw the scripts away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Ouais.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yeah.' Andréa gives a clipped, sullen answer.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "On a des nouvelles de cette Brancillon?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do we have news of that Brancillon?' Andréa asks whether there is any news yet from the potential buyer Brancillon.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Ça fait trois jours qu'elle n'est pas venue.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It has been three days since she came.' The time expression 'ca fait...",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Bizarre, non?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Strange, isn't it?' Camille remarks to Gabriel how strange Andréa's behavior is this morning.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Elle avait besoin de papiers.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She needed papers.' The imperfect idiom 'avoir besoin de' expresses a past need.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Elle n'a pas appelé?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She didn't call?' Remembering Andréa's midnight visit, Gabriel pretends everything is normal.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Non.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No.' Camille gives a clear and simple negative answer.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Je vous laisse.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I\\'ll leave you.' Sensing the awkward tension between them, Camille politely excuses herself.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Madame Brancillon!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Madame Brancillon! Wait!' Andrea calls out as the auditor marches past her office.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Je peux vous dire un mot?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Can I have a word with you?' Once they are alone, Andréa sheepishly asks Gabriel for a quick word. Now listen to the whole scene again at normal speed, and see how much more you catch.",
